ver  gonna be running through the same  dungeon twice per se you'll be in the  same area of course but never the same  layout are the same enemies essentially  now as a narrative designer how do you  approach pacing it was really difficult  with this one I got to give a lot of  credit to the rest of the team and the  artists and my co-workers being making  making sure the pacing is great because  as a narrative designer all I want to do  is sit and just like write write write  write write but this is a game where you  just want to get into it right so I  spend a lot of time axing words out of  narration so the main the main narrative  in the game and the main narrative  device is narration so none of the  characters have voice overs they all are  their story is told via narrator as if  it's like an old story in front of a  campfire kind of thing right so what was  the question  pacing so it just was important to make  sure that anytime we gave you a  cinematic it was short to the point and  it got the emotion across and the way we  kind of delivered all that was just  making sure that at key moments like for  instance beating a dungeon you were  given that and it's also important to  note that all those random encounters  they're all of the same quality is the  main narrative like they're all like the  same voice over  quality same cinematic value but it is  all completely random and not necessary  to see our do in order to complete the  game so the goal is to help hopefully  make sure that you're hitting enough of  those beats to make sure that you're  getting you feel like the world's  evolving around you so it's it's a  little bit of luck it's a little bit of  a making sure the random generator in  the game is giving you enough enough of  an option to pursue this additional  narrative how can people follow the  development of children more dead just  as kind of a lead out cool well we got a  website you can of course go check that  out we occasionally do blog pos